course: dictionary
lesson: 5034
title: Inject: to put in or to add
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inject means to put something into something else, often with a needle. «Nurses inject vaccines to protect us from diseases.» The nurse pushes the vaccine into your body, so inject means to put a medicine in.
explain: Inject can also mean to force a liquid or gas into something. «Stinging nettles have tiny hairs that inject a stinging liquid.» The hairs push the liquid into your skin, so the context tells you what inject means here.
explain: Inject can mean to add a new quality to something. «Inject some fun into the lesson» means make the lesson more fun. Check by swapping in a word: "put some fun into the lesson" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Inject is a verb: inject, injects, injected, injecting.
fact: An injection is a jab or shot given with a needle.
fact: «Inject» can mean to put medicine into the body with a syringe, as when nurses give vaccines.
fact: «Venomous snakes inject venom through fangs, mostly to catch prey.»
fact: Never touch a needle you find. Tell an adult straight away.
exercise: Nurses inject vaccines to protect us. What does inject mean here? | To wrap a bandage around an arm | *To put a medicine into the body with a needle | To cut the skin with scissors | To wash a wound with water
exercise: «Stinging nettles have tiny hairs that inject a stinging liquid.» What does inject mean? | *To force a liquid into something | To hide a leaf under the soil | To freeze water into ice | To pull a liquid out of something
exercise: Tom wants to inject some humour into his speech. What does he want to do? | To write the speech in capital letters | To read the speech out loud very slowly | *To add some humour | To remove all the jokes
test: A child finds a syringe in the park. What should they do? | *Tell an adult straight away and do not touch it | Hide it under a leaf | Put it in their pocket | Pick it up to see what it is
test: «Venomous snakes inject venom through fangs, mostly to catch prey.» Why do these snakes inject venom? | To wash their mouths | To make their fangs longer | To keep warm in the sun | *Mostly to catch prey
exam: Which sentence uses inject to mean add something new? | Snakes inject venom through their fangs | The nurse will inject the vaccine today | *«Inject some energy into the team talk» | The nettle hairs inject a stinging liquid into the skin
